So what does this all mean?

00:48:04.680 --> 00:48:05.680
Okay.

00:48:05.680 --> 00:48:07.680
So two key things.

00:48:07.680 --> 00:48:08.680
Okay.

00:48:08.680 --> 00:48:09.680
First thing.

00:48:09.680 --> 00:48:21.680
The fact that 80% of the time the S&P
barely moves makes it a lot harder to
generate returns.

00:48:21.680 --> 00:48:22.680
Okay.

00:48:22.680 --> 00:48:24.680
Especially when you account for
transaction costs.

00:48:24.680 --> 00:48:30.680
It means that our opportunities are
minimal when we're looking at daily
trading.

00:48:30.680 --> 00:48:33.680
Especially when the volatility's are low.

00:48:33.680 --> 00:48:34.680
Okay.

00:48:34.680 --> 00:48:38.680
And that's given by these average returns
that we looked at over here as well.

00:48:38.680 --> 00:48:39.680
The second thing is.

00:48:39.680 --> 00:48:41.680
Just something to be aware of.

00:48:41.680 --> 00:48:50.680
Is that by analyzing this distribution of
returns we can understand that there are
greater risks in the tails.

00:48:50.680 --> 00:48:51.680
In the extremities of the distribution.

00:48:51.680 --> 00:48:57.680
So they're actually more probable than you
might think.

00:48:57.680 --> 00:48:58.680
Okay.

00:48:58.680 --> 00:49:04.680
So that means there are likely to be days
when you'd be wiped out of your position.

00:49:04.680 --> 00:49:05.680
Of your account.

00:49:05.680 --> 00:49:06.680
Okay.

00:49:06.680 --> 00:49:18.680
So roughly one in a hundred days we've got
a fairly significant move of more than 3%.

00:49:18.680 --> 00:49:25.680
Which could wipe you out if you've got the
position on the wrong way.

00:49:25.680 --> 00:49:26.680
Okay.

00:49:26.680 --> 00:49:28.680
So they're the two major things.

00:49:28.680 --> 00:49:36.680
So the key thing we need to understand is
that this basically implies that
opportunities are minimal when there's low
volatility.

00:49:36.680 --> 00:49:44.680
The other thing just to keep in the back
of your mind is that there is greater risk
than predicted by normal distributions.

00:49:44.680 --> 00:49:56.680
And we should also point out that this
spreadsheet, you can apply this method to
any asset over any period, any frequency.

00:49:56.680 --> 00:49:59.680
So one week, like weekly, monthly, yearly
data.
